# Expectation record for 03_initializers/002_nested_aggregate.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_nested_aggregate
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Nested aggregate initialization -- struct within struct, struct within struct within struct, array of struct, and two- and three-dimensional arrays -- in fully braced, brace-elided and partially braced spellings, every member of every level read back individually, each shape declared once with static and once with automatic storage duration
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
A member or element left unmentioned by a brace-enclosed initializer is initialized as an object
of static storage duration would be, that is to zero, for automatic and static duration alike
(C11 6.7.9p19 and p21), so every value printed has a determinate value and no uninitialized
storage is ever read. Every fully braced object here is completely initialized, and every
brace-elided object supplies exactly as many initializers as the aggregate has scalar members, so
no slot depends on the zero guarantee either. Brace elision itself is well-defined C11 (6.7.9p20):
initializers are consumed from the flat list as the current object descends and ascends. Every
object is FULLY initialized by its initializer list before any part of it is read, and nothing is
modified after initialization: g_outer, g_arr, g_deep, g_matrix and g_cube at file scope with
their _flat and _partial twins, and l_outer, l_arr and l_deep inside main. No read of an
indeterminate value is therefore reachable, no object is modified twice between two sequence
points, and no modification races a read of the same object.
No arithmetic is performed on the initialized data at all, so no overflow of any kind is
reachable. The only arithmetic in the program is the loop counters' increments, every one of them
bounded by a literal of 2 or 3, so signed overflow is unreachable there too. Nothing is shifted,
divided or cast anywhere in the program.
Every subscript stays strictly inside its array bound, and each bound is a literal matching the
declared extent: g_arr is struct inner[3] read at 0 through 2, l_arr is struct inner[2] read at 0
and 1, both pair members are struct inner[2] read at 0 and 1, g_matrix is int[2][3] read at
[0..1][0..2], and g_cube is int[2][2][2] read at [0..1][0..1][0..1]. No pointer is formed anywhere
in the program, so no one-past-the-end pointer exists to be dereferenced, no pointer arithmetic is
performed, no address is taken and none is printed.
There is no aliasing violation: every value is read through an lvalue of its own declared type,
which is int in every case, reached by member selection and subscripting only. No object
representation is examined, no union appears, and no cast of any kind is present, so no
effective-type rule is approached. Only named members are ever read, never a padding byte -- and
these all-int aggregates carry no internal padding on any of the four targets in any case, so the
rule is honoured twice over, and nothing depends on the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
Every initializer value is a small positive int and the largest is 97, so every one is
representable in int on every target the suite supports and no implicit conversion changes a
value. Each object owns a disjoint value range -- 1 to 4, 10 to 31, 60 to 67, 71 to 74, 81 to 84
and 90 to 97 -- so a value that surfaces in the wrong place names the aggregate it escaped from
rather than merely reporting that something disagreed.
Each printf call receives at most one loop counter and one int member, neither of which has a side
effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. Every conversion specifier is %d and every corresponding argument has type int after the
default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by
the operating system. Nothing outside this file is read: every input is a literal here, no file,
socket, environment variable, clock, random source or locale is consulted, and iteration order is
fixed by literal loop bounds, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, and it builds and runs clean under
the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched. How the brace-elided spellings stay gate-clean without any flag change is recorded in
impl_defined_notes below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, no initializer spelling is
excluded, and no implementation-defined value reaches this program's output.
SCOPED DIAGNOSTIC PRAGMA, AND WHY THIS RECORD CARRIES NO ub_audit_flags DEVIATION. Brace
elision -- omitting the braces around a subaggregate's initializer, after which initializers
are consumed from the flat list as the current object descends and ascends -- is well-defined
C11 (6.7.9p20) but GCC reports it under -Wmissing-braces, which -Wall enables and the audit
gate's -Werror makes fatal. Five elided spellings were measured against the gate -- a
two-dimensional array written flat, a struct-in-struct written flat, a struct-in-array written
flat, an array-in-struct written flat, and a single-member struct written flat -- and every one
is rejected. There is therefore no spelling of this coverage that the unmodified gate accepts,
so the affected declarations -- and only those -- are bracketed in the source by `#pragma GCC
diagnostic push` / `ignored "-Wmissing-braces"` / `pop`, wrapped in `#if defined(__GNUC__)` so
a compiler that does not advertise GCC compatibility never sees them. This is deliberately NOT
a gate deviation: no command-line flag changes, so this program is audited with the suite's
DEFAULT full gate -- -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror,
every flag in force including -Werror -- and the ub_audit_flags key is absent from this record
by design. Nothing about undefined-behaviour detection is weakened: -Wmissing-braces reports
defined behaviour, not undefined behaviour, and the sanitizer gate
(-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all) runs unchanged and clean. Verified by
negative test: deleting the `ignored` line makes the gate fire again with
[-Werror=missing-braces], so the pragma is load-bearing rather than decorative.
This is the reason no constraint-C3 exclusion appears in this record. The alternative would have
been to drop the elided spelling and disclose the gap; a scoped pragma that changes no flag keeps
the spelling under test instead, which is what constraint C3 actually asks for.
WHY BRACE ELISION IS TESTED RATHER THAN EXCLUDED. It is a materially different path through the
initializer walker than the fully braced form, so a compiler can implement one correctly and the
other incorrectly. Each elided object is paired with a fully braced object of the SAME shape and
the SAME values -- g_matrix_flat with g_matrix, g_cube_flat with g_cube, g_outer_flat with
g_outer, g_arr_flat with g_arr, g_deep_flat and g_deep_partial with g_deep -- so the two paths
are compared against each other line for line as well as against this record. g_deep_partial is
the partially braced mixture, where the walker has to switch between guided and unguided descent
mid-initializer. The elision rule is exercised in two further places in this area, so the coverage
does not rest on this program alone: 007_string_array.c initializes char g_grid_exact[2][5] and
char g_grid_room[2][6] from unbraced string literals, which is brace elision for the inner arrays
and is gate-clean unaided because a string literal may initialize a character array without braces
(C11 6.7.9p14), and 003_partial_zero_fill.c's { 0 } idiom on a nested aggregate relies on the same
subaggregate-consumption rule of 6.7.9p20.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every object is a plain int printed with %d, so no type whose width differs
between the ILP32 target and the three LP64 targets ever reaches a format string, and no long,
size_t, ptrdiff_t, pointer or floating value is printed. i686 is ELF32 with a four-byte long and
pointer while x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 are ELF64 with eight bytes for both
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), a difference also MEASURED on all
four targets in this environment, and this program touches neither type.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. No character data appears at all, so the MEASURED split -- plain char
signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- cannot arise.
PADDING AND LAYOUT. Only named members are read, never an object representation, so no padding
byte is observed; these all-int aggregates carry no internal padding on any of the four targets in
any case, but the rule is honoured by construction regardless. No sizeof, no _Alignof and no
address is printed, so no layout choice the ABI is free to make is observable: only the values the
initializers supply are.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.
Nothing address-valued, clock-derived, random or locale-dependent is printed, and iteration order
is fixed. Every member of every level gets its own output line, 106 in total, and nothing is
summarized, so one divergent line localizes the defect to one initializer form; combined with the
disjoint value ranges, a value surfacing in the wrong place also names the aggregate it escaped
from.
THE DISCRIMINATING VARIANT in this area is the pairing of storage durations rather than a volatile
operand, and it is what makes the three optimization levels informative. An initializer for an
object of static storage duration is resolved before program startup and emitted into the data or
BSS image, whereas the automatic twin's initialization is a run-time act the backend performs on
entry to the block; with optimization off the statics appear as data-section bytes while the twins
appear as a run of stores into the frame, and at a higher level either path may be folded into
immediate operands. A compiler can implement one correctly and the other incorrectly, so both are
compiled at all three levels and their answers are printed separately, and a defect on one path
cannot be covered up by the other. A volatile operand would add nothing here, because the subject
is what an initializer produces rather than what an operator computes.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 106 lines byte-identically
with exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other
without any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record.
END
